managed_components/

# dependencies.lock stays ignored, and the reason is specific to this project
# rather than general.
#
# A lock file normally belongs in version control. Here it is per-TARGET
# state in a single file at the project root, and this repository builds two
# chips out of one directory -- so building the C5 to check it has not been
# broken re-resolves for esp32c5, empties managed_components/ and rewrites
# the lock. It was briefly tracked and what got committed was
# "target: esp32c5" with no dependencies in it at all: a lock file pinning
# nothing, naming the wrong chip.
#
# Versions are pinned where that cannot happen instead: exactly, in
# main/idf_component.yml, which is tracked and does not change with whichever
# board was built last.

